"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1JMAPP8SA1S0BQAJ\",\"title\":\"ZX-24 Vulkaneifel — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"VALIDATED\",\"EW\",\"ZX-24 Vulkaneifel\",\"ZeroEx\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Validated by\",\"EcoEngineers\",\"->\",\"Project code\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"K5SA\",\"approval\":\"28 Mar 2025\",\"protocol_current\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 3 of 3\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"28 Mar 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"28 Mar 2025\",\"Validation Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"19 Mar 2025\",\"Public Comment Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://zeroex.com\",\"t\":\"ZeroEx\"},{\"h\":\"https://ecoengineers.us\",\"t\":\"EcoEngineers\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/enhanced-weathering-agriculture/1.1\",\"t\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1J6CH94Q61S0DFA8\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6CH94Q61S0DFA8/prj_1JMAPP8SA1S0BQAJ/pjd_1JW8H8A431S050D1/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6CH94Q61S0DFA8/prj_1JMAPP8SA1S0BQAJ/pjd_1JR0MH8G71S0KP2D/validation_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6CH94Q61S0DFA8/prj_1JMAPP8SA1S0BQAJ/pjd_1JXW4NZ5X1S0ACD3/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nEW\\nZX-24 Vulkaneifel\\nZeroEx\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nValidated by\\nEcoEngineers\\n->\\nProject code\\nK5SA\\nApproval date\\n28 Mar 2025\\nCrediting period\\n23 Jul 2024 to 22 Jul 2029\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nEnhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\\nSummary\\n\\nZeroEx implements Enhanced Rock Weathering (ERW) projects in Germany, utilizing a basaltic rock powder byproduct from existing mining operations, and a novel, highly scalable MRV method that improves measurement accuracy and reduces costs. Through extensive exploration screening over 100+ quarries in Germany, ZeroEx has secured a steady supply of feedstocks with above-average CDR potentials and low concentrations of potentially toxic elements, ensuring compliance with Germany’s strict environmental regulations. By focusing on local deployments with transport distances under a 30 km radius from quarries, ZeroEx minimizes its projects’ carbon footprint while supporting local, family-owned farms to adopt sustainable practices. In 2024, ZeroEx spread 22,854 metric tons of basalt across fields of 18 partner farmers. The projects offer both socio-economic benefits as well as several agronomic advantages, including reduced emissions from traditional agricultural liming practices.\\n\\nEifel Region\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nEnhanced Weathering (EW) accelerates the Earth's natural chemical weathering process to remove carbon dioxide from the atmosphere. In chemical weathering, carbon dioxide dissolved in rainwater reacts with minerals in rocks, partly dissolving them and producing stable bicarbonate ions. These bicarbonate ions are transported by rivers to the ocean, where they are safely stored for thousands of years. EW is typically carried out by spreading crushed reactive rocks or minerals on croplands.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 2024\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2024\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2024\\nSite visit\\nCompleted 17 Apr 2025\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2025\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nInitial credit issuance\\n\\nIsometric issues credits to the project proponent. The results of the process, including the validation and verification report, will be made available for each project on the Registry.\\n\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n28 Mar 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n28 Mar 2025\\tValidation Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n19 Mar 2025\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 3 of 3\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"